course: dictionary
lesson: 1682
title: A name with a capital letter
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Christ is a proper name. A proper name is the name of one special person, place or thing, so it starts with a capital letter. Christ is a title for Jesus, and it means «the chosen one».
explain: Christians believe Jesus Christ is the Son of God, so Christ is at the centre of Christianity. The word also gives us Christian, Christianity and Christmas.
explain: Look at the words around it to find its meaning. «On Easter Sunday Christians greet each other "Christ is risen!"» shows a happy celebration. Some people also use «Christ!» as a swear word when they are shocked or angry, and many find that rude, so do not use it that way.
fact: Christ is a title given to Jesus by Christians; it means «the chosen one».
fact: «Christ» starts with a capital letter because it is a proper name.
fact: Phrases you may meet are Jesus Christ, before Christ (BC) and the life of Christ.
fact: Long ago people avoided holy names in anger, so «gosh» and «gee» stood in for God and Jesus, and «crikey» and «cripes» stood in for Christ.
fact: Galatians 3:28 says, «There is neither Jew nor Greek, slave nor free, male nor female, for you are all one in Christ Jesus».
exercise: «Christians believe Jesus Christ is the Son of God.» What does Christ mean as a title? | A type of church building | A king of a faraway land | *The chosen one | A pet name for a dog
exercise: Why do we write Christ with a capital letter? | Because it is always the first word of a book | *Because it is a proper name | Because every noun needs one | Because it sounds important
exercise: Which of these words comes from Christ? | Chapter | Chimney | *Christmas | Cheese
test: «Christians greet each other "Christ is risen!"» on Easter Sunday. What kind of greeting is this? | An angry shout | A rude swear word | A question about the weather | *A happy celebration
test: Which short form is used for «before Christ»? | RE | OK | *BC | PE
exam: Why should you not say «Christ!» when you are angry? | It is a title, so it means nothing | *It is a swear word many people find rude | It is the name of a church, so it is always wrong | It is too long to say quickly
